    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2505.13259v3-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Large Language Models (LLMs) are catalyzing a paradigm shift in scientific discovery, evolving from task-specific automation tools into increasingly autonomous <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> and fundamentally redefining research processes and human-AI collaboration. This survey systematically charts this burgeoning field, placing a central focus on the changing roles and&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2505.13259v3-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2505.13259v3-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2505.13259v3-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Large Language Models (LLMs) are catalyzing a paradigm shift in scientific discovery, evolving from task-specific automation tools into increasingly autonomous <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> and fundamentally redefining research processes and human-AI collaboration. This survey systematically charts this burgeoning field, placing a central focus on the changing roles and <span class="search-hit mathjax">escalating</span> capabilities of LLMs in science. Through the lens of the scientific method, we introduce a foundational three-level taxonomy-Tool, Analyst, and Scientist-to delineate their <span class="search-hit mathjax">escalating</span> autonomy and evolving responsibilities within the research lifecycle. We further identify pivotal challenges and future research trajectories such as robotic automation, self-improvement, and ethical governance. Overall, this survey provides a conceptual architecture and <span class="search-hit mathjax">strategic</span> foresight to navigate and shape the future of AI-driven scientific discovery, fostering both rapid innovation and responsible advancement. Github Repository: https://github.com/HKUST-KnowComp/Awesome-LLM-Scientific-Discovery.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2505.13259v3-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2505.13259v3-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 17 September, 2025; <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">v1</span> submitted 19 May, 2025;
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> May 2025.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">EMNLP 2025 Main</span>
    </p>
    

    

    
  </li>

  <li class="arxiv-result">
